ain-category/exalted/1262411-god-kicking-boots?p=1262811#post1262811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe evocations like Guile's &quot;sonic boom&quot; or Chun Li's &quot;really fast multi-kick (forgot it's name)&quot; or Liu Kang's &quot;bicycle kick&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one generally wants Evocations to be something other than just attacking with the weapon, to distinguish them from Martial Arts and native combat Charms.<br /> <br /> At least give it the force of some kind of principle or focused purpose.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T00:20:28-07:00","id":1263165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1262411-god-kicking-boots?p=1263148#post1263148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one generally wants Evocations to be something other than just attacking with the weapon, to distinguish them from Martial Arts and native combat Charms.<br /> <br /> At least give it the force of some kind of principle or focused purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The simpler artifacts tend to start enhancing attacks in thematic ways after all. <br /> <br /> Hmm. A god-kicking boot that lets an attack shockwave into onslaughting everyone at close range...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T21:23:38-07:00","id":1263738,"title":"","content":"People have been referring to Brawling, but there used to be leg/kick based Martial Art styles similar/based on capoiera or savate. After Kung Fu Hustle, I wanted to make a pair of PCs were one did musical attacks and support for the other, who danced and attacked to the beat. Had a partner for the plan, but 2.5 game fell apart. Alyways, what would make God-Kicking Boots better for MA as opposed to Brawling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like my Avatar? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T22:14:31-07:00","id":1263742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1262411-god-kicking-boots?p=1263165#post1263165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The simpler artifacts tend to start enhancing attacks in thematic ways after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I suddenly have the image of a 3-dot Artifact based around enhancement of kicking and stomping opponents in line with the image of the oppressive iron boot.<br /> <br /> Shock waves strike me either as the pinnacle Evocation of a 3-dot, or something around with to form a 4-dot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T03:58:19-07:00","id":1263761,"title":"","content":"Fist of the Titans is the big one here, I think. Shockwavy stuff make the core of its middle and late evocations, paired with stuff to weave them into big combos.<br /> So it might not need be a capstone. Might be one of the E2 openers and then worked with afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T07:31:19-07:00","id":1263790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1262411-god-kicking-boots?p=1263761#post1263761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fist of the Titans is the big one here, I think. Shockwavy stuff make the core of its middle and late evocations, paired with stuff to weave them into big combos.<br /> So it might not need be a capstone. Might be one of the E2 openers and then worked with afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, you're right of course. That one actually always struck me as interesting for both what it did, what was ascribed to it in legend, and still coming across as being 3-dot.<br /> <br /> I need to remind myself of my own standard that the dots are less about the basic form of the power, and more about the scope and structure of the Evocations. With that in mind, one could get a pair of boots based on providing some shockwave based enhancements to kicks and stomps, and another based on generating shockwaves in a manner that creates its own fighting style, and even one based on building up the energy to bring down mighty stomps that will level armies, cities and behemoths, and they'd all be quite different and make sense at their dot levels.<br /> <br /> (That and my perspective that you get variations in power even between Artifacts of the same level, even up to five dots; there are a few ways in which Stormcaller strikes me as a more sophisticated weapon than Soulfarer, which I find goes along with the latter being given an origin as having been made by some necromancer kings that probably weren't Exalted, while they still both fit the structure of five dots)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}